FarmtoPlate is setting up a blockchain product research and development team to deliver world-class enterprise grade Distributed Ledger Technology Networks for the food and beverage industry ecosystem. We are seeking an Associate DevOps Engineer with 2-3 years of experience to join our dynamic and innovative team. As an Associate DevOps Engineer, you will work closely with our development, operations, and infrastructure teams to enhance our cloud infrastructure and automate deployment processes. You will primarily be responsible for managing our AWS environment, implementing infrastructure-as-code using Terraform, and maintaining our Kubernetes clusters.
Job Description/ Responsibilities:
Design, deploy, and manage scalable and highly available AWS infrastructure using best practices and AWS services.
Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand application requirements and develop infrastructure solutions.
Develop and maintain infrastructure-as-code using Terraform, ensuring version control and documentation.
Monitor and optimize the performance, availability, and security of our AWS environment.
Automate deployment, configuration, and management tasks using CI/CD pipelines and scripting tools.
Implement and manage Kubernetes clusters, including deployment, scaling, and monitoring.
Troubleshoot and resolve infrastructure and deployment issues in a timely manner.
Collaborate with developers to streamline the software development lifecycle and improve efficiency.
Stay updated with the latest trends and technologies in DevOps, AWS, Terraform, and Kubernetes.
Requirements:
Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.
2-3 years of experience in DevOps or a related field.
Strong knowledge of Amazon Web Services (AWS) and its core services (EKS, EC2, S3, RDS, IAM, etc.).
Experience with infrastructure-as-code tools such as Terraform.
Proficiency in Kubernetes operations, including deployment, scaling, and monitoring.
Familiarity with CI/CD concepts and tools, such as Jenkins, GitHub CI/CD, or AWS CodePipeline.
Solid understanding of Linux/Unix operating systems and command-line tools.
Strong scripting skills (e.g., Bash, Python, or PowerShell) for automation.
Experience with containerization technologies like Docker.
Knowledge of networking concepts (VPC, subnets, security groups, etc.) and network troubleshooting.
Strong problem-solving and troubleshooting skills.
Excellent communication and collaboration skills to work effectively within a team.
Preferred Qualifications:
Familiarity with infrastructure monitoring and logging tools like CloudWatch, Prometheus, and ELK stack.
Experience with configuration management tools like Ansible or Puppet(optional).
